 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-tkb10P_5Xn4/WrOtDNa5OTI/AAAAAAAAJNk/vbTiD2Dbx7kM1vdm7hy1rvpbT3MIpcWZACLcBGAs/s1600/Example.jpg>

Now, I'm relatively new to IRT, but I believe that through using mirt, I can create 'item scores' based upon the hierarchical model defined earlier (for the moderator) and then use lavaan or MPlus to examine the moderated mediation model. Sort of an extension of what is done here <https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/jopy.12177>. If that is true, here is the part that I'm stuck on. What I would like to do is look at the lower order, 'medium order', and highest order facets for the moderator in separate analyses - essentially comparing the facet level results for the entire model to higher order results for the entire model - However, I'm unsure how to go about this. Specifically, is it better to estimate the item scores for each lower order facet individually? Or should I do all 6 at once?

Any guidance here would be greatly appreciated.

Best,

Chris

